From 789276bf39fe394905e273ecc987476879850181 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:34:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Grid mode: the survey as a programmable research grid
 (Phase 1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The second environment over the same survey. One row per question, one
column per thing a programmer scans for — where it sits, what it asks, what
it offers, what gates it, where it jumps, whether it is healthy, what it
reads and what reads it — and hundreds of them on screen at once.

It holds no survey data. Rows are derived from the store's definition on
every change (lib/grid/model.ts, pure, 12 tests), edits go through the same
engine functions and the same `update` as the Questions panel, and its
selection IS the Studio's selection: select a row and that question's
properties open on the right; switch back to Studio and you land on it.

  · Windowed by hand: `visibleRange` says which rows to mount for the
    scroll position, and only those exist. 600 questions cost the same as
    30 — 32 rows in the DOM, 413 ms to first paint, ~28 ms per long scroll
    step, 17 keystrokes in a cell in 273 ms. Status and dependency counts,
    the expensive layer, follow a deferred definition so typing never waits
    on them.
  · Sticky header, frozen status + ID columns, three densities, a column
    chooser (remembered per browser), sort by any header (ID sorts in flow
    order, not Q1 Q10 Q2), search across code / variable / text / options /
    logic, filters by type, block, "with logic", "issues".
  · Inline edit: text (plain only — markup and pipes open the Studio
    editor), variable (VariableNameInput: the same renameImpact →
    applyRename, the same refusals — a name a script depends on is refused
    with the engine's reason), type (useTypeSwitch, extracted from
    VariantSwitcher: the same migrateQuestionType and the same
    confirmation), required, block.
  · Multi-select with shift-range and ⌘-toggle via the shared selection;
    a bulk bar for required / optional / type (with a combined confirmation
    when any migration changes the answer shape) / move to block /
    duplicate / delete (referencesToMany preview, the same dialog).
    One ⌘Z takes a bulk edit back.
  · Keyboard: ↑↓←→ PgUp PgDn Home End Tab, Enter edits or opens, Space
    toggles, ⇧↓ extends, Delete deletes. Hover actions per row dispatch
    through the command registry with a context override.

Two things found and fixed on the way:
  · RightPanel's click-outside deselect fired on every grid click between
    pointerdown and click, wiping the anchor a shift-range needs. The grid
    owns its selection, so it is exempt.
  · The toolbar wrapped when the property panel opened, moving every row
    down a line under the cursor mid double-click. It no longer wraps.

Tests: lib/grid/model.test.ts (12), scripts/grid-mode-test.mjs (45,
including the 600-question budgets and a clean console). Mutation-checked:
windowing off, decoration off, range→select — each caught. Sweep green:
multimodal-foundation (updated: Grid is now built), context-right-panel,
properties-accordion, canvas (38), blocks, block-actions, save-integrity,
logic-builder, flow-dnd, variants-g5. Studio lib: 127.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
